              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Hindi for to feel, then the Hindi for to well up."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: आनंद",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "आनंद — ānand — \"joy; bliss\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "बच्चों के साथ खेलकर दादा को बहुत आनंद आया। baccoṁ ke sāth khelkar dādā ko bahut ānand āyā. Grandfather had a wonderful time playing with the children."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Masculine."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "आनंद (ānand) is a tatsama, borrowed from Sanskrit ānanda, \"happiness, joy\" (Monier-Williams). ānand ānā, \"joy comes\", is how Hindi says someone enjoyed a thing."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for describing what you lived and felt."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
